      {"id": "R-SIGN-NAMING-W4-2-SIDE", "layer": "FEDERAL", "ta_id": null, "jurisdiction": null, "topic": "sign_size", "strength": "OPTION", "text": "The MUTCD names the Lane Ends sign W4-2 with no side (Table 6H-1, Sect. 6H.08). The pack uses W4-2R (Figure 6P-33, right lane closed) and W4-2L (TA-33 note 1, left lane closed); both take the W4-2 size row (owner-approved interpretation). The side naming itself is not in the MUTCD.", "condition": null, "action": null, "value": null, "value_max": null, "unit": "in", "qualifier": null, "status": "SOURCE_REVIEW_REQUIRED", "sme_question": "The MUTCD has one Lane Ends sign, W4-2, with no side suffix. The pack calls the right-lane version W4-2R and the left-lane version W4-2L (the mirror image, per TA-33 note 1 'the corresponding Lane Ends signs'). Are W4-2R and W4-2L the codes your drafts and sign supplier use, and is W4-2L the mirror image of W4-2R?", "interpretation": null, "source_ref_ids": ["SR-6H08-P01", "SR-6H1-W4-2", "SR-6P33-N1", "SR-6P33-FIG-SIGNS"]},
